  "result": "Perfect! The enhanced `renderInvoiceText` function is working beautifully. Here's a summary of the improvements:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully polished the `renderInvoiceText` function in `src/render.js` with comprehensive enhancements:\n\n### New Features Added:\n\n1. **Line-level Discounts**: Each line now shows its discount percentage and amount in parentheses (e.g., `(10% off: -\u20ac10.00)`) when a discount is applied\n\n2. **Voucher Display**: The voucher code and amount are displayed just before the total line (e.g., `Voucher (WELCOME10): -\u20ac10.00`)\n\n3. **Due Date Line**: When an invoice has a `dueDate`, it's displayed after the total (e.g., `Due: 2026-10-31`)\n\n4. **Payment Tracking**: When an invoice has payments, the total amount paid is displayed at the end (e.g., `Paid: \u20ac80.00`)\n\n### Output Structure:\n```\nInvoice Number / DRAFT\nCustomer Name\nLine Items (with discounts shown inline)\nSubtotal (if applicable)\nDiscount\nVAT\nVoucher (if any)\nTotal\nDue Date (if applicable)\nPaid Amount (if applicable)\n```\n\n### Test Coverage:\nAdded 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Line discount display (both explicit and tier-based)\n- Voucher visibility and formatting\n- Due date presence and formatting\n- Payment amount calculation and display\n- Proper sequencing of elements\n- Complete invoice rendering with all features\n\n### Test Results:\n- **All 427 tests pass** (414 before + 13 new render tests)\n- Full backward compatibility maintained\n- Realistic demonstration shows all features working together\n\nThe enhanced invoice rendering now provides complete visibility into invoice details including discounts, vouchers, payment history, and due dates!",
